play:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;} That centers content vertically, filling. Hmm but requirement says \"通过增加行距与间距、并将底部英文标签贴底对齐来填满\". So increase line-height and gaps.\n\nApproach: card-body {flex:1; display:flex; flex-direction:column; justify-content:space-between? } Not quite; for c1 two elements, space-between would push key to top and subline to bottom — too far apart maybe fine actually. Better: use padding/gaps.\n\nLet me do: .card-body{flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;gap:...}\n\nLet's set:\n- c1: key line-height 1.6, sub-line line-height 2.0, margin-top 26.\n- c3: note line-height 2.0, marker margin-top auto? marker inside card-body.\n\nLet's compute c1 body content target ~168px:\nkey 36*1.6 = 57.6\nsub-line margin-top 26 + 17*2.0=34 → 60\ntotal ~118. Centered with justify-content:center leaves 25px top/bottom — acceptable, looks filled.\n\nc3: note 21*2.0=42 (one line, actually \"创新性结论需在试验完成后检验。\" one line, width 552-76=476px, font 21 → ~14 chars fits in one line? 21px chars ~ 21*14=294, yes one line). marker margin-top 20 + ~31 = 51. total ~93. Hmm smaller. To fill: center it. Maybe increase spacing: note line-height 2.2, marker margin-top 34.\n\nActually to visually fill, centering is the cleanest. Use justify-content:center for card-body, and add extra spacing so content block is a decent size.\n\nCard heights equal 320 → bottom aligns at 832. Footer rule at 960, fine.\n\nLet me also ensure card padding bottom leaves foot at bottom: card-foot margin-top:auto.\n\nLet me write CSS changes:\n\n.card{... height:320px;}\n.card-body{margin-top:22px;flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;}\n\nFor c1: .card-body .key line-height 1.6? Keep 1.45 maybe but add gaps.\n\nI'll write per-card tweaks:\n\n.c1 .card-body{justify-content:space-evenly;} hmm.\n\nSimpler and robust: give each card-body justify-content:center; and set gaps:\n.c1 .key{line-height:1.5;}\n.c1 .sub-line{margin-top:30px;line-height:2.0;}\n.c2: strong line-height 1.6; mini-rule margin 26px 0; note line-height 1.9.\n.c3: note line-height 2.0; marker margin-top 32px.\n\nAlso c2 body content: strong 25*1.6=40; mini-rule 1 + margins 52 = 53; note 21*1.9=40 → 133, centered.\n\nc1: 54 + 30 + 34 = 118.\nc3: 42 + 32 + 31 = 105.\n\nReasonable. Maybe pull closer to full: for c3, add more line-height 2.2 → 46; marker margin-top 40 → 117.\n\nFine. Let's write final HTML with only style changes.\n\nAlso marker has display:inline-block and margin-top:20px; inside flex column it becomes flex item; align-self:flex-start needed so it doesn't stretch. Add .marker{align-self:flex-start;} Actually inline-block in flex container becomes block-level flex item stretching full width. Set align-self:flex-start to keep border hugging text. Good.\n\nAlso .mini-rule in flex column: height 1px, flex-shrink 0.\n\nWrite final."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10377,"completion_tokens":5153,"total_tokens":15530,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":5888},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1180},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":5888,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":4489},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}